    "result_text": "I added `check_super_user` to `lnbits/decorators.py`. I haven't run any code or tests, so it's untested.\n\nThe admin endpoints in `lnbits/core/views/admin_api.py` already used it. `admin_api.py`, `user_api.py`, `node_api.py` and `lnbits/__init__.py` all import it, so no endpoint edits were needed. The function was missing from `decorators.py`, which would have made those imports fail.\n\n**What it does:** it resolves the logged-in account with `check_account_exists` and raises 403 unless the account is the configured super user. It also raises 403 if the account has no password configured, matching `check_admin`.\n\n**Pattern use:** I based it on the catalog pattern `auth.check_admin@v1` and kept its `# pcat:` marker. I dropped the \"or in `lnbits_admin_users`\" part of the check, because you asked for super user only. `check_code` reports no high-severity deviations, only low ones: the error messages and the narrower condition. No `pcat-allow` approvals were needed.\n\n**Where it's used:**\n- `api_delete_settings`\n- `api_restart_server`\n- `api_download_backup`\n\nThe other admin endpoints still use `check_admin`, so regular admins keep access to them. If you want any of those moved to super-user-only, tell me which."
